* ascended a vampire-lord healer yesterday


So... I wonder what would you say about ascending a non-humanoid monster?  
I guess someone already thought about the idea, I just can't seem to find 
any YAAPs nor even any midgame discussion.  Browsing the rgrn archives 
turned up an 'initpoly' patch from somewhere in 2002, however, I didn't 
notice anything being said about post-mines experiences.  That patch would 
make the beginning simply trivial while removing the possibility of 
preparation in my stock-binary strategy of polying in the midgame.

My own thoughts are:
* unless you're a gray dragon, you _have_ to wish for the EotW, PYEC, EotA 
  (neutral) or OoDet, SoMight or MMoMerlin (lawful), and they can't be 
  your quest artifact as whatever can steal it can touch you the very next 
  round.  Somehow, SoMight works when carried while Magicbane doesn't.
* for anything with a bite attack (ie, most viable mons), you'll want to
  genocide c and N (not strictly mandatory, but...)
* curses will be a royal pain
* regeneration is mandatory (you regenerate only 1hp/20turns when polyed)
* a ring/amulet eating spree before the final poly is close to a must -- 
  or a must for non-pacifist purple worms
* if anything important falls into a pit, you lost if you can fly (there 
  is no way to intentionally descend into one)


============================================================================
Back to ordinary humanoid monsters:
* ascending a xorn is FUN.  You can use everything but shirts, body armour 
  and cloaks (-> no magic cancellation), but if you have free action, 
  walking through walls more than makes up for that restriction.  While 
  still low on hp (I didn't know of alchemy then) you'll need to hide in 
  the walls a lot, but later, just imagine going through Gehennom...
  Xorns also have pretty unique diet of platemails, rubber chickens, rings 
  sometimes even a wimpy food ration.  I just don't see how the DevTeam 
  could fail to give an YAFM when eating cockatrices...
* arch-liches are fun, but nowhere close to xorns.  Their carrying 
  capacity is halved compared to humans, and being undead means !pray 
  (unless you're chaotic -- I wasn't).  Too bad, your extra attack is cold
  instead of death...
* vampire lords have great natural AC, fly and have a bite drain level 
  attack (hard to believe, but I really _did_ unintentionally hit a 
  cockatrice after polying but before switching my AoLS to the AoUC.  Pure
  luck...).
  Having innate flying is extremely unbalanced, too.  I personally believe
  that intrinsic (non-mounted) flight should be _blocked_ by encumbrance
  instead of negating most of its negative effects.
  For a healer, the SoA+2nd attack combo means that most monsters die due
  to drainage instead of real damage...


